Run the fixtures matrix and write a scorecard

Usage:
  eval [flags]
  eval [command]

Available Commands:
  check       Lint the fixtures; exit 1 when one is malformed
  compare     Compare two sets of trajectory files offline
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  diff        Compare two scorecards; exit 1 when the new one is worse
  help        Help about any command
  replay      Print the spans a run recorded, gate spans with their triggered flag
  stats       Summarise trajectory files offline

Flags:
      --agent string      agent preset name, never a model name (required)
      --arm strings       arms to run: preset, control (bare-bash baseline) (default [preset])
      --fixtures string   directory of fixtures (default "evals/fixtures")
      --format string     edit format axis, e.g. diff or whole
  -h, --help              help for eval
      --out string        directory the scorecard is written to (default "evals")
      --packs string      packs lock file the run used, e.g. factory.lock
      --redo              rerun tickets --run-dir already finished
      --replay            re-score the outputs stored in --run-dir without dispatching
      --run-dir string    keep results and trajectories here so a killed run resumes
      --tries int         tries per ticket; the scorecard gets pass_rate_1..N (default 1)
      --workflow string   workflow name (required)

Use "eval [command] --help" for more information about a command.
